From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:40:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2: use PHY RX delay

The Zero2 describes its RTL8211F link as plain "rgmii" with the whole
RX clock delay (3100 ps, the maximum the H616 EMAC syscon can add)
inserted by the MAC. With "rgmii" the realtek PHY driver also clears
the PHY's own RXDLY bit (page 0xd08 reg 0x15 bit 3), so RX sampling
relies on the MAC delay alone and sits at the edge of the window.

On a board this shows up as intermittent dead-RX boots, cold and warm:
link up at 1000/full, frames transmitted and seen by the peer, but
rx_pkt_n stays 0 and the EMAC interrupt never fires for RX. All EMAC
clock, pinmux, drive and syscon registers are identical between good
and bad boots. On a bad boot, setting PHY RXDLY and the syscon ERXDC
field to 0 restores RX instantly without a link reset.

Use "rgmii-rxid" (PHY inserts the RX delay, MAC none) as the Orange Pi
Zero3, with the same PHY and layout, already does upstream, and as the
vendor BSP does (rx-delay = 0, PHY strap delay). The TX delay stays at
700 ps.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -18,9 +18,8 @@
 };
 
 &emac0 {
-	allwinner,rx-delay-ps = <3100>;
 	allwinner,tx-delay-ps = <700>;
-	phy-mode = "rgmii";
+	phy-mode = "rgmii-rxid";
 	phy-supply = <&reg_dcdce>;
 };
 
